# Testing and Verification

- Write one focused failing test before implementing new behavior, then verify
  the expected failure and the passing result.
- Use unit tests for mechanics, integration tests for complete rounds/games,
  and deterministic seeded tests for randomness.
- Test public behavior and legal transitions rather than implementation details.
- Keep training and evaluation tests separate; use small fixtures and bounded
  runs.
- Run `uv run pytest`, `uv run pyright`, `uv run ruff check .`, and
  `uv run ruff format --check .` as appropriate.
- On Windows use `scripts/check.ps1`; on Linux/macOS use
  `bash scripts/check.sh`.
- Do not claim a test, build, or workflow passes without fresh command output.
